AIPSTER Worker for Debian/Ubuntu
-------------------------------

First run creates the private per-user data directory
~/.local/share/aipster-worker (or $AIPSTER_WORKER_DATA) holding
config.toml, api-token.txt, pairing.json, state/ and logs/. Upgrade,
removal and even purge preserve it; to delete it manually, stop the
worker first (`aipster-tray quit`) and remove that directory.

The tray (`aipster-tray`, also in the applications menu) owns one local
worker plus the account-pairing heartbeat sender. Pairing never starts
anything by itself: mint a one-time code in the dashboard (My Compute,
Pair this computer), then use the Pair button (or `aipster-worker pair`).

The worker starts nothing on login by default. To start the tray on
login: `aipster-worker autostart on`. To stop: `aipster-worker
autostart off`.

The bundled engine is simulated: `/api/jobs` stays disabled and
heartbeats prove reachability only, never inference readiness.
